Specularity
===========

Specularity is an original, clean-room implementation. It was inspired by, and
reproduces a similar feature set to, Stefan Minning's *Normality* plugin for
Adobe After Effects (Normality © 2009 Stefan Minning, https://www.minning.de).

Specularity shares NO source code with Normality. It was not decompiled,
disassembled, or derived from the original binary. All shading math is a fresh
implementation of standard, publicly documented computer-graphics techniques
(Lambert diffuse, Blinn-Phong specular, Schlick Fresnel, matcap/environment
mapping, etc.). Names of observable UI features (parameter labels, display and
blend modes) describe standard techniques and are used descriptively.

PBR pass names and conventions (Source, BaseColor, Roughness, Metallic,
Specular, Alpha, Depth, Normal) follow the Beeble PBR export format
(https://beeble.ai) and are used for interoperability.

The Adobe After Effects SDK is required to build this project and is NOT
included or redistributed here. Obtain it from the Adobe Developer Console.

